#!/bin/sh
cat <<'MSG'

mali-vendor-krane installed. Two things are still needed:

  1. The driver itself. It is under ARM's EULA and cannot be shipped, and the
     only Mali-G72 build for Linux is ChromeOS's. Fetch one:

         sudo mali-vendor-setup

     That downloads the recovery image for this board, reads it as it comes
     and keeps only the root partition, then removes it again.

  2. This project's kernel package, which carries the kbase module and a
     second set of device tree blobs describing the GPU the way kbase wants
     it. mali-vendor-setup switches /etc/deviceinfo over to them.

Panfrost and kbase claim the same device tree node, so only one of them can be
bound at a time. Going back is one line: drop the deviceinfo_dtb override and
run mkinitfs.

MSG
exit 0
